   "text": {
    "L1": "Weather is the condition of the air at a place for a short time, such as hours or days.",
    "L2": "Climate is the average weather pattern of a place over a long time, about 30 years or more.",
    "L3": "The Sun heats land and sea unevenly. Land heats faster than water.",
    "L4": "Warm air over the land rises, making lower pressure. Cooler air over the sea has higher pressure.",
    "L5": "Air moves from high pressure to low pressure. This movement is wind, not trees waving their branches.",
    "L6": "Weather has several elements, including temperature, pressure, wind, humidity, rainfall and clouds.",
    "L7": "Each element can be measured: a thermometer measures temperature, and a barometer measures air pressure.",
    "L8": "A rain gauge measures rainfall, while an anemometer measures wind speed and a hygrometer measures humidity.",
    "L9": "At the beach, this process makes a cool sea breeze during the afternoon. At night, the breeze reverses.",
    "L10": "Now put the steps of the afternoon sea breeze in the correct order."
   },
